# Backend rules (`server-v2/`)

## 🔴 Row-level security (the #1 gotcha)
- Tenant tables have **FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY**. Raw `getDb()` reads/writes
  return 0 rows / throw unless wrapped in `withWorkspace(workspaceId, db => …)`
  (sets `app.workspace_id` via `SET LOCAL`).
- Cross-tenant work: enumerate `workspaces` (NOT RLS'd) then `withWorkspace(ws.id)`.
- NOT RLS'd (safe with raw `getDb`): `workspaces`, `users`, `user_sessions`,
  `messages`, `campaign_steps`, `proxies`, `plans`.
- The app DB user has **no DDL rights** — don't add migrations expecting
  `npm run migrate` to alter schema as that user.

## Scheduler & worker
- **The scheduler tick is the backbone** — scheduled jobs are drained there, not
  inline. Without the worker, sequences never advance past day one.
- **Pacing deferrals `return`, never `throw`** (throwing burns all 3 BullMQ
  attempts in the blocked window). Call `pacing.release()` on defer/failure.
- Commit "sent" BEFORE ancillary writes (idempotent, no double-send).

## Conventions
- `@/` alias → `server-v2/src/*`. Every service touching tenant tables uses `withWorkspace`.
- Kysely increment in `onConflict`: `eb('col','+',n)`.
- Validate inputs (`class-validator` / explicit guards); throw `BadRequestException`
  with a user-safe message.
- Never connect the app to a Supabase **transaction pooler** (:6543) — it breaks
  `SET LOCAL` used for RLS. Use session pooler / direct (docs/adr/0001).
